      "text": "To find the product of the two numbers, let's denote them by \\(a\\) and \\(b\\). We know two things about these numbers:\n\n1. The least common multiple (LCM) of \\(a\\) and \\(b\\) is 36.\n2. The greatest common divisor (GCD) of \\(a\\) and \\(b\\) is 6.\n\nThe relationship between the LCM and GCD of two numbers \\(a\\) and \\(b\\) is given by the formula:\n\\[\n\\text{LCM}(a, b) \\times \\text{GCD}(a, b) = a \\times b\n\\]\nSubstituting the given values into this formula, we get:\n\\[\n36 \\times 6 = a \\times b\n\\]\nCalculating the left side, we have:\n\\[\n36 \\times 6 = 216\n\\]\nTherefore, the product of the two numbers is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{216}\n\\]",
